\ul{
\li{Every configuration keeps the eight cores busy (CPU over wall clock 6.3 to 7.7, reachability less): the cold run is bound by CPU, as the warm pass is ([the profile of the default configuration](rep-P11)). A cold JVM spends its extra CPU compiling: 24.7 s against 4.5 s on Init, 124.5 against 109.2 s on Mathlib; with the AOT cache 12.5 and 114.3 s.}
\li{\strong{Memory}: the executable holds less on every corpus: 370 against 726 MiB on Init, 3,645 against 4,829 MiB on Mathlib.}
}

\p{The wall clock of a process that is not the check: the process's wall clock minus what the checker itself reports with \code{\verb~|--stats~}, in milliseconds - the start of the runtime before \code{main} and the exit after the verdict.}

